00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:42.990
That's Nathan voice.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:43.990
That's Nathan Fillion?

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:44.990
Yeah.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:45.990
It's just his voice.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.360
I don't know if he did any motion capture
work for it, but it is his voice.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.360
Yeah.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.360
I had no idea.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:52.150
He was like back in the days friends with
James Gunn.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:55.099
Because he did Slither but he also did PG
Porn.

00:05:55.099 --> 00:05:56.099
Yeah, exactly.

00:05:56.099 --> 00:05:57.099
Wow.

00:05:57.099 --> 00:05:58.099
Hilarious.

00:05:58.099 --> 00:05:59.099
I didn't know that.

00:05:59.099 --> 00:06:00.099
Yeah, that's a funny video.

00:06:00.099 --> 00:06:01.099
Yeah.

00:06:01.099 --> 00:06:02.099
Nathan Fillion.

00:06:02.099 --> 00:06:03.110
Tiny little MCU cameo dude.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:07.860
That does seem like the easiest possible,
like, nerd cred thing that we could do, right?

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.719
Is just get the entire cast of Firefly back
together.

00:06:10.719 --> 00:06:15.119
Just bring everyone back now that Joss Whedon
is out of the picture.

00:06:15.119 --> 00:06:16.449
Just bring...just make Firefly part of the
MCU.

00:06:16.449 --> 00:06:17.900
Oh, don't make it weird.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:18.900
Yeah.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:19.900
Yeah.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:20.900
Just make Firefly MCU Canon.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:24.199
I mean Disney owns it now, right?

00:06:24.199 --> 00:06:25.199
Yeah.

00:06:25.199 --> 00:06:26.199
It's Fox.

00:06:26.199 --> 00:06:27.490
Bring it back.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:30.169
Anyway, we've gotten off topic.

00:06:30.169 --> 00:06:35.720
So for me, the two actors that I...I wrote
a few different actors down that I really

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:36.939
like.

00:06:36.939 --> 00:06:42.330
But the two that I was happiest about, I also
got their roles in mind.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:45.340
And it's Richard Ayoade, from The IT Crowd.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.340
Love him.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.340
Cool.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.099
I want him to play Mr. Fantastic in the Fantastic
Four movie.

00:06:50.099 --> 00:06:51.099
Interesting.

00:06:51.099 --> 00:06:54.539
And America Ferrera, from Superstore.

00:06:54.539 --> 00:06:57.860
And I want her to be the Invisible Woman.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:02.779
And I want to see what they're like, because
Richard Ayoade is very good at being intelligent

00:07:02.779 --> 00:07:06.750
and aloof and funny and charming all at the
same time.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:12.300
And America Ferrera is good at being tough
and caring and powerful and bringing a bunch

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:15.430
of weirdos together to get stuff done, from
Superstore.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:16.430
Great show.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:20.969
So I just think that if you stick those two
together, you bring life to these two parts

00:07:20.969 --> 00:07:27.599
that in the past, again, the previous Fantastic
Four movies...there's some good stuff, there's

00:07:27.599 --> 00:07:28.899
some not so good stuff.

00:07:28.899 --> 00:07:35.729
But overall I would say that the dynamic between
Mr and Ms Fantastic has not necessarily been

00:07:35.729 --> 00:07:38.149
all that interesting or exciting.

00:07:38.149 --> 00:07:39.900
Would you say it has not been fantastic?

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:49.449
It has not been marvelous, or fantastic, or
amazing, or spiderman.

00:07:49.449 --> 00:07:53.629
But I think that...and I'm not necessarily
saying that these two actors have like such

00:07:53.629 --> 00:07:54.629
great chemistry.

00:07:54.629 --> 00:07:55.629
I have no idea.

00:07:55.629 --> 00:07:57.389
But they're interesting choices.

00:07:57.389 --> 00:08:01.620
They're choices that I don't think I ever
would've thought of if I hadn't been asked

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:06.979
this question, and I think I would love to
see something...everyone talks about John

00:08:06.979 --> 00:08:10.419
Krasinski and Emily blunt as the two leads
of the Fantastic Four.

00:08:10.419 --> 00:08:12.987
And it's like, sure. Why not. Fine. Okay.

00:08:12.987 --> 00:08:15.149
Yeah. I mean that would work.

00:08:15.149 --> 00:08:16.986
Yeah. It's fine.

00:08:16.986 --> 00:08:19.739
Like they're great. If they got cast tomorrow, I'd be like yeah.

00:08:19.739 --> 00:08:22.454
Cool, okay. I'll see that movie.

00:08:22.454 --> 00:08:26.449
I actually just watced Quiet Place for the
first time this weekend, Because I am really

00:08:26.449 --> 00:08:27.449
easily frightened.

00:08:27.449 --> 00:08:29.720
So, that was not something I went into lightly.

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:32.060
They're very good at it.

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:35.229
Like, they're great actors and they work beautifully
together, obviously.

00:08:35.229 --> 00:08:38.930
So yeah, I'd be psyched, but let's go for
maybe a less obvious choice.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:41.010
Let's just try something a little different.

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:45.720
And plus, Emily Blunt recently, at least at
the time at the time of this recording, recently

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.860
was like, "stop asking me about it.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.860
Kind of sick of hearing about it.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:51.209
I don't think I'm going to do it."

00:08:51.209 --> 00:08:53.170
So I'm kind of like, all right, cool.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:55.430
So let's find and talk about someone else.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:56.440
So let's make this happen.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:59.209
Like Richard Ayoade and America Ferrara.

00:08:59.209 --> 00:09:00.209
Why not?

00:09:00.209 --> 00:09:01.430
They're very...

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.300
Really talented people.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:06.779
And you were like "I don't know if they'd
work well together", but here's why I think

00:09:06.779 --> 00:09:14.370
they might, is they're both trained comedic
actors who have worked with...their resumes

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:15.370
are very ensemble based.

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:18.690
I mean, American Ferrera did the Sisterhood
of the Traveling Pants movie, she did Ugly

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:20.180
Betty, she did Superstore.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:24.620
Richard Ayoade has done...the IT Crowd is
very much based on riffing off one another

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:25.620
and the chemistry, right?

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:29.639
So they're both people with experience in
working with ensembles and making that work.

00:09:29.639 --> 00:09:32.149
So I think they could be great together.

00:09:32.149 --> 00:09:36.540
And Richard Ayoade has already worked with
Disney in the Star Wars universe doing the

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:39.769
voice of that robot, from Mandalorian.

00:09:39.769 --> 00:09:42.690
The one whose name we all remember.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:44.040
It's a bunch of numbers and letters.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.040
It's numbers.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:46.040
That's fine.

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:47.040
And then he was also in Soul.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:48.279
Everybody's name is a bunch of numbers and
letters.

00:09:48.279 --> 00:09:49.589
He was in Soul.

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:51.940
I forgot he was in Soul.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:56.100
I think overall at the very least, I really...I'm
excited about that idea.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.300
I'm like...in my head now it's already happening.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:01.329
But it's just kind of like, what would that
be like?

00:10:01.329 --> 00:10:02.509
And he could keep his British accent.

00:10:02.509 --> 00:10:04.810
I don't want to hear him doing an American
accent.

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:06.800
Make him British, who cares?

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:08.120
Just go with it.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.449
It'd be interesting.

00:10:09.449 --> 00:10:13.259
Brian, can I ask you who would play Ben Grimm
in your version?

00:10:13.259 --> 00:10:16.920
I didn't think that far ahead, but I do think
you could just get Michael Chiklis back.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:19.009
Can I make the recommendation?

00:10:19.009 --> 00:10:20.009
Sure.

00:10:20.009 --> 00:10:22.560
Rowan Atkinson.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:25.360
Perfect.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:27.639
Who's going to play the human torch?

00:10:27.639 --> 00:10:28.870
Probably also Rowan Atkinson.

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:29.870
He's got a lot of...

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:30.870
Rowan Atkinson is a good choice.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:32.000
He contains multitudes.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.030
Yeah.

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:35.209
You know who could be a really good thing?

00:10:35.209 --> 00:10:36.680
Jesse Plemons.

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:37.680
Oh.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:38.680
Yeah.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:40.839
He's a bigger dude.

00:10:40.839 --> 00:10:42.689
He's not known for his small stature.

00:10:42.689 --> 00:10:47.279
He's a big presence, and he's got...he's an
incredible actor.

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:49.759
